menu "libjpeg-turbo"

    config LIBJPEG_TURBO_ALLOC_PREFER_SPIRAM
        bool "Prefer PSRAM for libjpeg-turbo allocations"
        depends on SPIRAM
        default y
        help
            Route libjpeg-turbo's memory manager (jpeg_get_large() and
            jpeg_get_small()) to PSRAM first. Internal 8-bit RAM is used as a
            fallback when PSRAM is not initialized or cannot satisfy an
            allocation.

            Large objects (sample rows, coefficient buffers, virtual arrays)
            take most of the memory an encoder or decoder needs, so moving them
            frees the most internal RAM. Small pools hold the per-image control
            structures and Huffman/quantization tables.

            Without this option libjpeg-turbo calls malloc(). With
            CONFIG_SPIRAM_USE_CAPS_ALLOC, malloc() never returns PSRAM; with
            CONFIG_SPIRAM_USE_MALLOC, only requests above
            CONFIG_SPIRAM_MALLOC_ALWAYSINTERNAL do.

            PSRAM is slower than internal RAM, so encode and decode run slower
            with this option enabled.

endmenu
